# Paths excluded from `bun run scan:secrets` — and from NOTHING ELSE.
#
# This file has exactly one reader: the `scan:secrets` script in package.json,
# which is a manual, on-demand full-repo scan. It is not run by CI and not run
# by the pre-commit hook. Specifically:
#
#   - CI (.github/workflows/secret-scan.yml) runs the trufflesecurity/trufflehog
#     action against the PR diff with `--results=verified,unknown`. It passes no
#     `--exclude-paths` and never reads this file.
#   - The pre-commit hook (lint-staged -> scripts/secret-scan.sh) scans only the
#     staged paths it is handed. It never reads this file either — despite its
#     own failure message telling you to "add the path to .trufflehog-exclude",
#     which does nothing for the hook. Use SKIP_SECRET_SCAN=1 for that path.
#
# The previous header here claimed "CI and the pre-commit hook honor the same
# set." Neither did. Adding a path below suppresses it in `bun run scan:secrets`
# only.
#
# One glob per line.
node_modules
dist
dist-build
dist-release
.claude/worktrees
.claude/logs
bun.lock
